The following uses or conditions shall be and are hereby prohibited within wellhead protection zones, whether or not such use or condition may otherwise be ordinarily allowed within the zoning ordinance but for the prohibitions under section 26-54 of this article:
(a) Any new septic tanks or drain fields appurtenant thereto may not be less than 250 feet from the wellhead;
(b) Sanitary landfills including but not limited to solid waste landfills, industrial waste landfills and construction/demolition waste landfills;
(c) Hazardous waste disposal sites;
(d) Any new storm water infiltration basins within 250 feet of the wellhead;
(e) Any new underground storage tanks within 250 feet of the wellhead;
(f) Any new sanitary sewer lines within the control zone of a wellhead.
(g) Animal feedlots, poultry enclosures, or animal enclosures (this prohibition shall not be construed to apply to family pets) within 250 feet of the wellhead;
(h) Agricultural waste impoundments;
(i) Land application systems of waste water or sludge.
(Ord. No. 2018-1009A, 10-9-2018)

